---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/kit/PageHeader.astro";
import DraftNotice from "../components/kit/DraftNotice.astro";

export const prerender = true;

/*
 * DRAFT, NOT LEGAL ADVICE. Needs review by a Philippine lawyer before launch.
 * Confirm before launch:
 *   - the legal entity and its registration (not registered yet)
 *   - partner pricing, refunds and cancellation (the business model is pending)
 *   - VAT and invoicing obligations
 *   - the licence a venue grants over its scan, and what happens on cancellation
 *   - liability limits enforceable under Philippine law
 */
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of use" description="The terms for using Visita, as a visitor or as a venue owner.">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10">
    <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms of use" lede="The terms for using Visita, whether you're looking for a cafe or listing one." />
    <div class="prose-visita">
      <DraftNotice>These terms are a working draft and haven't been reviewed by a lawyer yet. They will be finalised before public launch.</DraftNotice>

      <h2>1. What Visita is</h2>
      <p>
        Visita publishes real 3D scans and details of cafes so you can see a place before you go. Unless a listing says otherwise, we aren't affiliated with the
        cafes we list and we don't run them.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Using Visita</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use Visita lawfully and don't interfere with how it works or how it's secured.</li>
        <li>Don't copy, scrape, republish or resell our scans or listings without written permission.</li>
        <li>Don't post content that's unlawful, misleading, or infringes someone else's rights.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Your account</h2>
      <p>You sign in with Google and are responsible for activity on your account. You can close it at any time.</p>

      <h2>4. Reviews and photos</h2>
      <p>
        You're responsible for what you post. By posting, you let us show it on Visita. We may remove content that breaks these terms, isn't a genuine account of a
        visit, or is the subject of a valid complaint. We never write reviews ourselves and never publish invented ones. Venue owners can't review their own venue.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        A scan shows a room as it was on the day it was captured, and rooms change. Amenity details come from the venue and from visitors. Where we don't know
        something we show nothing, but we can't guarantee every detail is current, so check anything you're relying on.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Venue owners</h2>
      <p>
        If you list a venue, you confirm that you manage it, that you're allowed to have it scanned and published, and that the details you give us are accurate.
        Owner accounts are approved manually. Changes to verified amenities are reviewed before they appear. Fees, billing and cancellation are set out in your
        partner agreement. We may decline or withdraw a listing, including where information turns out to be inaccurate.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Scans and trademarks</h2>
      <p>Scans we capture remain ours; your listing lets us show them on Visita and anywhere else we agree in writing. Your trademarks and branding stay yours.</p>

      <h2>8. Availability</h2>
      <p>Visita is provided as it is. We don't promise it will always be available, and features may change.</p>

      <h2>9. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent Philippine law allows, we aren't liable for indirect or consequential loss from using Visita. Nothing here limits liability that the law says
        can't be limited.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of the Philippines, with venue in the courts of Cagayan de Oro City.</p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms: <strong>hello@visita.ph</strong>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
